HISTORICAL INITIAL TEMPLATE/LAYOUT REFERENCE
This document preserves the original development table and its pinned hashes.
Its old hosted arena/output sizes are not the current compiler contract.
Use compiler.zero, LANGUAGE.ztext and selfhost/CORE.ztext for current capacities,
Windows/guest targets and later native-template overrides.

Zero IA32 and real-mode code-generation layout

Contract
--------
All source assets are Zero statements. The caller declares @templates pointing
to 128 zeroed entries of 16 bytes. Each template entry stores an ASCII lowercase
hexadecimal string pointer at +0 and its decoded byte count at +8. Decode two
characters per byte. Empty or absent entries must not be treated as supported
operations. The entry_arguments template for IA32 is intentionally empty.
The largest string is 1024 characters (512 decoded bytes); every string stays
below Zero's 4095-character limit.

These tables describe our existing instruction encodings, not a copied compiler
executable. The existing built compiler is only the bootstrap provenance. Table
extraction and verification did not invoke an assembler or linker.

